      "chatGptNotes": "Content and umlaut checks approved from accepted review ledger mathematik-batch-105.md (accepted_pilot). Review note: The image correctly treats the discontinuity at `x=0` for `f(x)=1/sqrt(x)` as a one-sided limit: `integral_0^1 1/sqrt(x) dx = lim_{a->0+} integral_a^1 x^(-1/2) dx = lim_{a->0+}(2-2*sqrt(a)) = 2`. It clearly marks the finite area result and does not substitute directly at `x=0`.",
